aints or not  let's turn to saint isador who currently  has the marvelous title of patron saint  of the internet  so for someone who is the heavenly  advocate of the internet  sin isidor never even touched a computer  born in the year 560  he would predate the launch of the  internet by 1429 years  bear in mind that he was 610 years off  the invention of the wheelbarrow which  was first recorded in europe  in 1170. the reason why saint isidore  got connected to the internet is his  ambitious quest to compile  all the world's knowledge into a single  book known as the etymology  it is a 20 book compendium with  everything from metallurgy  medicine to mathematics it's during this  work where he also invented the full  stop  comma and colon so if you ever get  caught up by tricky punctuation  it's this person to blame with the dawn  of the internet in the early 90s  humanity entered an unprecedented age  where information could be accessed  instantly  this is especially true with the launch  of wikipedia on the 15th of january 2001  which currently has 6 million articles  in english the site is an online  database  which possesses all of human knowledge  gained thus far  so too was saint isidore's etymology  because of this association  the saint quickly became viewed as the  patron of the internet  his enthusiasm for knowledge was  allegedly noticed by pope john paul ii  who reportedly declared him to be a  saint of all things digital  in fact using the internet i found this  prayer for saint isidore  it's a prayer asking for protection from  the internet  grant we beseech thee that through the  intercession of saint isidore  bishop and doctor during our journeys  through the internet  we will direct our hands and eyes only  to that which is pleasing to thee  and treat with charity and patience all  those souls whom we  encounter i don't know about you but  this saint seems to be the catholic  church's alternative  to anti-virus software there is only one  problem  wh